<p>At least 25 people were killed and dozens injured in a stampede at the Citadelle Laferrière, a historic mountaintop fortress near Milot in northern Haiti, during annual festivities over the weekend, according to Haitian authorities and multiple news reports. Haiti later declared three days of national mourning, and the Haitian National Police opened an investigation into the incident. The disaster struck one of Haiti&#x27;s most important national landmarks, adding to the shock around the event.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NKJ2X-hpnJE1Rhb2Z9NzeWjz3lwWPed0RITPKEDEN2xZpfVaUrEGwU5hwrNHnk3W7fx8Yq6CE3J-jBPBDDlQpGJUuoQOeRaZtLgD266srg7MAzZcLXMBwWgUBoaOu95IYURsIftE9VG9tI8N9jo2vOCImJF8c4b5vi-FlWXhiyFxMr-isUyGEWq1K4NXQhYidvI7-H4-V3QIVw' alt='The Citadelle Laferrière, a large 19th-century fortress in northern Haiti, in 2024.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Crowd trigger: The New York Times reported that the tragedy unfolded around the appearance of a social media personality at the fortress celebration, adding a possible crowd-management dimension to investigators&#x27; work.</li><li>Fatality revision: Authorities later revised down an earlier, higher death toll, underscoring how difficult it was to confirm casualties in the immediate aftermath.</li><li>Naming variations: Reports referred to the monument as Citadelle Laferrière, Citadelle Henri and Citadelle Henri Christophe, reflecting the different names used for the same fortress.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/stampede-haitian-mountaintop-fortress-reportedly-leaves-30-dead-131965172'>Stampede at Haitian mountaintop fortress reportedly leaves at least 25 dead</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/haiti-declares-three-days-of-national-mourning-for-25-killed-in-stampede'>Haiti declares three days of national mourning for 25 killed in stampede</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/12/worl